    {
      "id": "1cd7897b-52d2-4c2e-a430-561b06fd839e",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 912,
        "content": "## Track contract e-signatures, generate onboarding checklists, and catch stalled deals\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow tracks contract e-signature events from a webhook, validates the request, and updates Airtable records when contracts are completed. It uses an LLM to generate an onboarding checklist, then sends follow-up emails, Trello tasks, and Slack notifications, including escalation for high-value contracts. A separate scheduled branch runs daily to find contracts that have stalled and alerts sales in Slack.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the contract-signing webhook URL in the e-signature platform and set the matching shared secret token in the configuration node.\n- Connect Airtable credentials and set the correct base ID, table name, and field mappings for contract lookup, status logging, and CRM updates.\n- Configure the Groq chat model credentials and verify the structured checklist parser matches the expected onboarding checklist format.\n- Connect Gmail, Trello, and Slack credentials, then set the destination email settings, Trello list ID, and Slack channel/user targets.\n- Set the daily schedule and stale-days threshold for the stalled contract monitoring branch.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the high-value contract condition, onboarding checklist prompt/output schema, stale contract threshold, and notification destinations to match your sales and onboarding process."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c200a153-016f-456d-bd87-b2bf5a00b895",
